Rule 1 (dataset must be a tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= v_1 ≠ None
>>
Rule 3 (If the dataset has an empty repeat count, its cardinality is unknown)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if v_1 = 0 then v_1 = 0
>>
Rule 4 (dataset cardinality must be positive.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= v_1 > 0
>>
Rule 5 (Check the type of the tensor which contains dataset)
{v_1 : tensor} |= v_1 = 1
>>
Rule 6 (The tensor input parameter should not be a string)
{v_1 : tensor} |= v_1 ≠ "ii" ∨ v_1 ≠ "ii->i" ∨ v_1 ≠ "i,j->ij" ∨ v_1 ≠ "bij,bjk->bik" ∨ v_1 ≠ "...ij->...ji" ∨ v_1 ≠ "bn,anm,bm->ba" ∨ v_1 ≠ "none" ∨ v_1 ≠ "sum" ∨ v_1 ≠ "max" ∨ v_1 ≠ "min" ∨ v_1 ≠ "prod" ∨ v_1 ≠ "relu" ∨ v_1 ≠ "tanh" ∨ v_1 ≠ "sigmoid" ∨ v_1 ≠ "softmax" ∨ v_1 ≠ "elu" ∨ v_1 ≠ "selu" ∨ v_1 ≠ "gelu" ∨ v_1 ≠ "swish" ∨ v_1 ≠ "softplus" ∨ v_1 ≠ "linear" ∨ v_1 ≠ "valid" ∨ v_1 ≠ "same" ∨ v_1 ≠ "causal" ∨ v_1 ≠ "channels_last" ∨ v_1 ≠ "channels_first"
>>
Rule 7 (dataset should not be float)
{v_1 : tensor} |= v_1 ≠ 0.1 ∨ v_1 ≠ 0.2 ∨ v_1 ≠ 0.3
>>
Rule 8 (dataset length)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 1 ∨ v_1.len = 2 ∨ v_1.len = 3
>>
Rule 9 (dataset dim)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 2 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 3
